 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "roomba e5 wont charge properly, sometimes it does sometimes it doesnt"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Intermittent charging issues with Roomba E5 units are most commonly caused by dirty or oxidised charging contacts on either the robot or the home base, rather than a failed battery. Please switch off and unplug the home base from the wall before checking. Look at the gold metal strips on the bottom of the vacuum and the pins inside the dock; if they look dusty or green/corroded, gently clean them with a dry cloth or a cotton bud dipped in a little isopropyl alcohol (ensure everything is completely dry before plugging back in). Also, ensure the power cable connecting the base to the wall is seated firmly at both ends. If cleaning the contacts and securing the cables doesn't resolve it, we may need to look at the battery health or the charger itself."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Did that. Contacts on the dock were dull with a greasy grey film and loads of hair round the ones on the robot. Wiped them and it's charged 4 nights running now, no error. No heat or smell from it either. Is that it sorted?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, it sounds completely sorted. The fact that it has charged reliably for four nights without any error codes or overheating suggests that the dirty contacts were the only issue. To help keep this up, I’d suggest giving those charging pins a quick wipe with a dry cloth once every month or so to stop dust and hair building up again. If you need anything else, just let me know."
  }
 ],
